CM_ SG_ 124 Y_COMPANION_RAW "Three separate fields. Bit 77: set when Y >= 0 (inverse of Y sign bit 76 on 99.3-100%), redundant. Bits 78-79: life state 0 newborn, 1 established, 2 ending (2 on 6-26% of a track last three frames vs 0.1-4% mid-life, ten recordings).";
CM_ SG_ 124 VELOCITY_CANDIDATE_RAW "Working decode vRel = 0.1*(raw-1539) m/s (accepted). Raw 0 (-153.9 m/s) is a floor saturation seen on newborn far objects, not a sentinel.";
CM_ SG_ 124 LATERAL_VELOCITY_CANDIDATE_RAW "Lateral velocity 0.1*(raw-511) m/s, positive left, relative in the sensor frame (includes the apparent motion of stationary objects from ego yaw). Provisional 2026-09-28: local Y slope and gyro kinematics on held-out recordings, zero 510-511 on stationary scenes; one held-out bracket (0.1004-0.1085) misses 0.1.";
CM_ SG_ 124 NORMALIZED_RATE_CANDIDATE_RAW "Bosch A NORMALIZED_CLOSING counterpart (provisional). 0.001*(raw-40000) 1/s, approximately vRel/(dRel+2.3 m); follows Doppler vRel, not range change. 64999 = invalid, with TTC 0, TTC sigma 0 and normalized-closing sigma 0 in the same frame.";
CM_ SG_ 124 QUALITY_CONTAINER_RAW "Bits 144-153 (upper byte always 0). Bosch A RANGE_SIGMA candidate (provisional): range-noise specific on 8 of 10 recordings, weak (partial rho 0.08-0.25). Strongly range dependent. Units unknown. No validity gate.";
CM_ SG_ 124 REL_VELOCITY_UNCERTAINTY_CANDIDATE_RAW "Bosch A REL_VELOCITY_UNCERTAINTY counterpart (accepted, raw units): velocity-noise specific and monotonic with empirical vRel noise on ten recordings. Nonlinear in m/s; 1023 may be saturation.";
CM_ SG_ 124 UNCERTAINTY_160_CANDIDATE_RAW "Mostly 1-2; higher on young and laterally offset objects. Weak noise association. Units unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 124 ACQUISITION_186_CANDIDATE_RAW "Starts near 23 on newborn tracks and decays to about 2. Carries little information beyond track age.";
CM_ SG_ 124 UNCERTAINTY_192_CANDIDATE_RAW "Decays with age; mixed velocity and lateral noise association, not specific to one noise. Units unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 124 TTC_CANDIDATE_RAW "Time to collision (provisional), (raw-1024)/128 s, equal to -1/normalized closing within 0.06-0.10 s median where that is under 7 s. 2046 = not populated (no closing within about 8 s); 0 = invalid (normalized closing 64999). No Bosch A counterpart.";
CM_ SG_ 124 TTC_SIGMA_CANDIDATE_RAW "TTC uncertainty (provisional): raw = TTC^2 * NORMALIZED_CLOSING_SIGMA / 64 within 0.1-2.5% on ten recordings. 127 = saturated or not populated; 0 = invalid. Stays populated on 3-26% of frames where TTC is defaulted (TTC about 8-19 s).";
CM_ SG_ 124 WIDTH_FINE_258_CANDIDATE_RAW "Angular extent measure, about 1/range within a track. No fixed affine relation to the azimuth-edge width. Units unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 NORMALIZED_CLOSING_SIGMA_CANDIDATE_RAW "Bosch A NORMALIZED_CLOSING_SIGMA counterpart (accepted, raw units): specific to normalized-closing noise and monotonic with it on ten recordings; tied to TTC_SIGMA by a fixed 1/64 ratio. 0 when normalized closing is invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AUX_LATERAL_MOTION_304_CANDIDATE_RAW "Signed 16-bit two-complement. Follows lateral motion; scale unresolved (brackets 0.005-0.12 m/s per count). -1 when normalized closing is invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AUX_LATERAL_DIRECTION_320_CANDIDATE_RAW "Set when AUX_LATERAL_MOTION_304 is nonnegative on 97-99% of observations.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AUX_328_CANDIDATE_RAW "Changes nearly every frame; weak association with lateral and angular noise, not specific to one. 0 when normalized closing is invalid. Meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AUX2_378_CANDIDATE_RAW "Signed 13-bit. Shares one subrecord with bits 480-487: both hold their defaults together (8190 here, signed -2; bits 480-487 zero) on about two thirds of observations. When populated, values follow the azimuth sign. Meaning unresolved; the earlier 384:7 probe is this field sign extension.";
CM_ SG_ 124 MATURITY_398_CANDIDATE_RAW "Counts down from about 6 to 1 as a track matures. Adds no velocity-error or survival information once track age is known. Upper-bit semantics unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AZIMUTH_CENTER_CANDIDATE_RAW "Unsigned, zero at 4096, positive left, 2^-12 rad per count (+-1 rad span; within 0.97-1.03 on nine recordings with 0.01 m lateral). Equals the midpoint of the two edge fields on 97-99.9% of observations.";
CM_ SG_ 124 AZIMUTH_EDGE_A_CANDIDATE_RAW "Left angular edge; same encoding as AZIMUTH_CENTER. Always at or left of the center. Clips at 8191 (+1 rad).";
CM_ SG_ 124 AZIMUTH_EDGE_B_CANDIDATE_RAW "Right angular edge; same encoding as AZIMUTH_CENTER. Clips at 0 (-1 rad) for near objects at the field-of-view edge. The edge difference is the Bosch A ANGULAR_WIDTH counterpart: it scales as 1/range within a track (log-log slope -0.91 to -0.99, ten recordings).";
CM_ SG_ 124 MOTION_CLASS_CANDIDATE_RAW "Observed 0, 2, 4. 4: same-direction traffic, and most objects seen only while ego is stopped. 2: oncoming or approaching, and most stationary objects seen while ego moves. 0: unassigned; young tracks, and every object on the 2026-09-10 and 2026-09-16 drives. Not a validated classifier.";
CM_ SG_ 124 ANGULAR_WIDTH_COARSE_CANDIDATE_RAW "Angular extent measure, about 1/range within a track. Not a fixed-scale copy of the edge width (forward vs inverse fits 6-21 vs 14-24 edge counts per unit). Not received power.";
CM_ SG_ 124 ANGULAR_WIDTH_COARSE_COPY_CANDIDATE_RAW "Byte 61 equals byte 59 on 99.7-100% of observations.";
CM_ SG_ 124 FLAG_106_CANDIDATE_RAW "Set on about 40% of newborn frames and 97-99% after 1 s; agrees with Y_COMPANION bit 78 on 96%. Meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 FLAG_107_CANDIDATE_RAW "Set on 0-3% of observations, mostly mature same-direction movers. Meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 ENUM_109_CANDIDATE_RAW "Values 0-4. 1 on most established tracks; 2-4 mostly on same-direction movers near the path with high existence. Not an object class (metric width about 1.7 m for all values) and not a left/right lane code. Meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 124 EXISTENCE_PROBABILITY_CANDIDATE_RAW "Bosch A OBJECT_EXISTENCE_PROBABILITY counterpart (accepted, raw units). 0-49 only, 49 most common. Best survival predictor within range x age strata on ten recordings (AUC 0.67-0.92); falls over the last second before track death; low on short-lived ghosts. 0 marks degraded measurement (large range and velocity steps). Probability scale unresolved.";
BA_ "VFrameFormat" BO_ 126 14;
CM_ SG_ 126 CRC16_RAW "Capture-verified CRC16: polynomial 0x1021, init 0xFFFF, no reflection or xorout; bytes 2:64 then little-endian data ID 0x0fb9.";
CM_ SG_ 126 OBJECT_ID_RAW "Observed 0 empty, 1 through 63 active. IDs move between wire slots and are reused.";
CM_ SG_ 126 LIFECYCLE_RAW "Observed +3 modulo 4096 per consecutive sweep for continuing IDs. Resets or discontinuities require a new track.";
CM_ SG_ 126 POSITION_X_RAW "Unsigned. Working decode dRel = 0.05*(raw-4096)-4.296 m (accepted). Normalized closing and azimuth both imply a sensor range origin about 2.3 m behind the dRel origin.";
CM_ SG_ 126 X_COMPANION_RAW "Values 0, 1, 3, 4 only; rarely changes within a track. Value 1 coincides with one-step range jumps on 5 of 10 recordings only. Meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 126 POSITION_Y_RAW "Signed 13-bit two-complement, positive left. Working decode 0.01 m/count (accepted 2026-09-28; gyro, camera and azimuth-field consistency). 8191 encodes -1 and is not an invalid sentinel.";
